  "body": "The cost-63 P111 decoder is known, but its source access, asymmetric COPY\nendpoint, exact phase frame and dirty restoration need a physical word. This\nPR adds a complete finite complex decoder and an executable coordinate\nbaseline with the same 674 original streams and physical endpoints. The sole\nnonzero COPY endpoint is processed last. All source reads, adapters, copy\nlifetimes and three unused rank-nine helper tails are paid.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899/research/shared-carrier-decoder/PROOF.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899/research/shared-carrier-decoder/EXPECTED.json) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899/research/shared-carrier-decoder/SOURCES.json).\n\nThe complete recursive profile changes from\n`896 H1 + 444 H7 + 238 H8` to\n`945 H1 + 497 H7 + 182 H8 + 3 H9`. An exact uniform inequality proves a smaller\nrecursive moment for `0 <= b <= 1/256`, including the selected complex\nexponent at the pinned base. **The candidate also costs 108 more AXPY scans,\n126 more dyadic scalar multiplications per address, and 392 more adapter\nscans.** This is a construction and a recursive-cost comparison; it is not a\nruntime gain, selected-supplier improvement, or new kappa.\n\nThe proof binds each logical event to its exact live Clifford frame. It proves\nthe complete physical map and its inverse transpose, including allocation and\ndisposal of the one temporary stream. Dirty helpers recover their logical\ninputs at FULL, so their physical outputs are F times their initial arrays.\nThey are not claimed to have physical identity endpoints.\n\nValidation uses exact rational replay of all 674 independent logical columns,\na separate integer-column interpreter, every native phase and child rank,\nfour whole physical executions on 512 complex addresses per role, and every\nmatrix column of the rank-seven COPY. Eleven broken-word controls address\ncompensation, cleanup, source access, endpoint order, helper tails, temporary\nlifetime, phase and recursive charge. Three further controls reject a missing\nreceipt and Boolean or float substitutions for integer receipt fields. Normal\nand optimized relocated replays passed, as did a changed-source rejection and\nthe selected-record check. The coordinator separately replayed a second dense\ninput in both candidate orientations. Reproduction is:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/shared-carrier-decoder/verify.py\npython3 -I -B research/shared-carrier-decoder/test_controls.py\n```\n\nThe exact Gaussian physical replay is finite. A written composition proof\nsupplies its all-input conclusion. The package gives a conservative quadratic\nfinite tape-route bound; it does not claim the all-size linear tape, rounding,\nside-correction, external endpoint, host-owner or outer-assembly obligations.\n\nThe new work is confined to [research/shared-carrier-decoder/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899/research/shared-carrier-decoder) at base\n[8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20). Selected and upstream files stay\nunchanged. [PR #717](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/717) and [PR #968](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/968) receive credit for the complex decoder and the\ncopy-cost result; [PR #620](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/620), [PR #757](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/757), [PR #761](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/761) receive related depth-one credit. [PR #998](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/998),\n[PR #1008](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1008) and [PR #1020](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1020) concern different structural classes and do not supply this\nphysical construction. The exact compiler is retained and pinned from\n@icekylinx's [PR #531](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/531) lineage. Prepared for Ali Romman (@aliromman) with substantial\nOpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0. No independent human review is claimed.\n",
